      "dom_id": "question-87221",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Compute $P(X<-5)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{4x},\\, & x\\le 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & x>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<-5) & =P(-\\infty <X<-5) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{-5}4{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[{e}^{4x}]}_{-\\infty }^{-5} \\\\  & ={e}^{-20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
